<title>HONG KONG: Earthquake rocks Japanese islands - HK officials.</title>
<headline>Earthquake rocks Japanese islands - HK officials.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>An intense earthquake estimated at 5.5 on the Richter scale shook the area around the Ryukyu islands of Japan, the Hong Kong Royal Observatory said on Monday.</p>
<p>The epicentre of the quake, detected at 11.06 p.m. Hong Kong time (1506 GMT) on Sunday, was initially determined to be about 280 km (170 miles) northeast of the Japanese city of Okinawa. The observatory gave no further details.</p>
</text>
